WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:02.760
Captain Marvel has started her descent.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:07.419
The trailer for the 21st entry in the Marvel
Cinematic Universe has arrived with explosive

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.260
style, and we couldn't be more excited.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:14.140
So suit yourself up in mohawk mode, and follow
along as we break down all the little details

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.640
in the first trailer for Marvel's Captain
Marvel.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.420
Psyche-magne-fragilistic-expialidocious

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.650
In the comics, Carol originally received her
powers by being caught in the blast of an

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.349
exploding psyche-magnetron ...whatever that
actually is.

00:00:28.349 --> 00:00:31.940
At the time, Carol was the head of security
on a US Air Force base.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.260
In the trailer, Carol can be seen in an Air
Force jumpsuit, looking roughed up in the

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.500
desert, potentially having just had her plane
shot out of the sky.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.860
Soon after, she's enveloped in some fancy
blue light an all-time classic giveaway for

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.520
Made-Up Powerful Comic Book Energy.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:50.031
Is this the movie version of the exploding
psyche-magnetron, altering Carol's DNA to

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.520
give her her powers after crashing to the
Earth during a Kree-Skrull dogfight?

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:54.200
Maybe!

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.320
Ronan... we meet again?

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.100
The trailer features a familiar silhouette
for MCU fans: sure looks a lot like the return

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:05.180
of Ronan the Accuser, back to life in Captain
Marvel through the magic of the prequel.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.160
This time, the former Guardians of the Galaxy
bad guy technically should be on the side

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:13.040
of the good guys with Carol, considering his
status as a Kree in the Kree Empire.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.400
In the comics, Ronan attempted to overthrow
the Kree Empire, bringing him into conflict

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.120
with Mar-Vell.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:21.740
Whether or not that conflict will be repeated
in this movie remains to be seen.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:23.980
Origin stories

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.980
Carol Danvers' isn't the only origin story
the Captain Marvel movie appears to be remixing.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:33.430
The movie also seems to be seeding a whole
new origin story for another hero once known

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:34.900
by the name of Captain Marvel.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.480
The trailer shows a chummy relationship with
Carol Danvers and another Air Force pilot

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.979
by the name of Rambeau, most likely a reference
to Monica Rambeau, a Marvel Comics character

00:01:43.979 --> 00:01:48.180
who technically was the first female Captain
Marvel, taking the name well before Carol

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:51.350
did, since Carol first went by the super-name
Ms. Marvel.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.160
Comics are weird.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.100
All that said, this is not Monica, but rather
a young version of Maria Rambeau Monica's

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.600
mother.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:01.680
Because this movie's a prequel, we may meet
Maria's daughter Monica at some point in this

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.460
film...or maybe in a future sequel or spin-off.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.720
There are some Marvelous possibilities...

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.780
Skrull and crones

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:13.280
Everyone's going to walk away from this trailer
talking about one moment:

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:17.860
But as you probably suspected, not all is
how it seems.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.810
We're pretty sure the main bad guys of the
movie will be the Skrulls, an intergalactic

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:24.460
warrior race that once did battle with the
Kree.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.500
They've pestered Marvel's superheroes for
years with their numerous attempts to invade

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.000
Earth.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.900
The Skrulls appear just before the old lady
in the trailer, implying a connection between

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:33.400
the two.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.300
As you might have surmised, the Skrulls are
shapeshifters, being in their basic forms

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.460
humanoid aliens with reptilian or goblin-like
qualities.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.260
So are there secret, shapeshifting Skrulls
already lurking in the Marvel Cinematic Universe?

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.580
This movie sure seems to make that a safe
bet...

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.480
Target acquired

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.950
Captain Marvel is putting Marvel's de-aging
CGI to work to spectacular effect on Samuel

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.520
L. Jackson's young, bicloptic Nick Fury, agent
of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.620
From the look of things, Young Fury will spend
the first act of the movie working to track

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.110
Carol Danvers down after she busts open that
Blockbuster.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:07.760
But will they be friends...or foes?

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.020
Fury's pager has the answer, as he sends the
message, "With Target"... which is kinda far

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:13.760
off from "With my new pal, Carol."

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.680
We know from the end of Infinity War that
the two end up at least as pen pals, but it

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.300
will be interesting to see if they face any
opposition from each other on their way to

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.580
becoming best buds.

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:24.840
Big guns and green guys

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.140
Finally, the first Captain Marvel trailer
also features what appears to be a scene of

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:33.470
Roswell-esque alien dissection, with what
looks like a Skrull's body lying prone on

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:38.140
an operating table while a scrubbed-up doctor
digs in and a G-man-looking gentleman looks

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:38.640
on.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.980
Also present in the shot: Nick Fury, holding
what appears to be, from this distance, a

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.480
purple space bazooka.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.340
And an icepack...on his eye...

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.810
The arrival of the Skrulls on Earth in the
'90s raises a lot of questions about the MCU

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.300
of the now.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.540
The movie will certainly explore their shapeshifting
powers, and the eerie implication is that

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.260
there could be spies from another galaxy all
over the MCU we know.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:03.280
How much do you want to wager that the next
big Marvel guessing game will be "what heroes

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:05.459
have been secret Skrulls this whole time"?

